The vapor pressure of benzene and toluene at 20$^{\circ}$C are 74 and 22 torr, respectively. A certain solution of both at 20$^{\circ}$C has a vapor pressure of 50 torr. Assuming the mixture is ideal,
\begin{inparaenum}[(i)]
\item     calculate the mole fraction of benzene in the mixture. %0.54
\item     calculate the mole fraction of toluene in the mixture. %0.46
\end{inparaenum}
